Hello there,
Could you please provide an example on how approximate GP model is used in C++ environment?
I encountered segment fault during ".forward()" part.
torch_model_ = torch::jit::load(torch_model_file);
std::vectortorch::jit::IValue torch_inputs;
torch_inputs.push_back(torch::ones({50, 1, 5})); // window_size, batch_size(single data point), input_dimension
auto torch_output = torch_model_.forward(torch_inputs);
Do I need to include extra files, such as inducing points, when using approximate GP model in c++?
Thanks!

Is it possible to fix lengthscale but optimize other hyperparameters?
I found a similar question in #689 and I tried
optimizer = torch.optim.Adam([
{'params': model.likelihood.parameters()},
{'params': list(set(model.covar_module.parameters()) - {model.covar_module.base_kernel.lengthscale})}
], lr=0.1) but the lengthscale was still being optimized. Is there a solution to this? Thank you!
